    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218-a14">

                <pb facs="0378" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg282"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 131.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ethéart to Mr. Bassett</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            3, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch of yesterday’s date, relating to the Jastram affair, the
                    contents of which dispatch I hastened to communicate to the council of
                    secretaries of state.</p>
                <p>My colleague of the department of interior, who is charged to order a new inquiry
                    into this affair, will not fail to obtain the result of this investigation,
                    which he expects to receive on the arrival of the post from the north, due here
                    at this moment; in which case I will have the honor to respond in a definite
                    manner to your aforesaid dispatch.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, Mr. Minister, to accept the renewed assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. ETHÉART.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
